[S] YAAP long and probably spoily.

My first post to this newsgroup. An ascension of a neutral human
Valkyrie in slashem-0.0.7E6F1.

I have ascended Valkyries, barbarians and a tourist in nethack. This
is my first slashem ascension. In general I find slashem to be much
harder than nethack. My subjective impression is that the monsters are
tougher, and there seem to be a lot more of them. In addition,
slashem seems to be gratuitously nasty at times. Slashem forces you to
play carefully and conservatively, traits which I suspect will have
improved my vanilla nethack play. For this ascension I found
Eva Myer's slashem spoilers
(http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/index.html) useful, and I
looked at the source a fair amount too.

I have found it difficult for valkyries to survive in slashem without
an early altar for Mjollnir. This game gave a co-aligned altar on
level 2, so away I went with Mjollnir. This alter became my base for
the rest of the game. The minetown altar was co-aligned. So after
clearing the mines and a refreshingly difficult unspoiled sokoban (got
an "oR) I was well away. There were no significant bones in the game.

Down to the castle there was no real danger, and using a magic lamp from
minetown I wished for gauntlets of power. Of course, gauntlets of
power turned up a couple of levels later. I used the magic lamp from
the sunless sea as a light source for the rest of the game.

Before Gehennom I went up and down the dungeon doing the special
levels and quests. None of this was any real problem. Vecna died to a
single blow of Vorpal Blade, and Lord Surtur was a walkover. The
nightmare level was irritating, but again, no real danger. The "guild
of disgruntled adventurers" took several passes to clear. There were a
number of /of draining in the hands of adventurer monsters. I find it
a little inconsistent that these are not stopped by reflection. It
makes the game more challenging, but IMO does not follow "nethack
logic". IMHO draining should be stopped by magic resistance or
reflection, or both and so is an example of slashem nastiness.

I never found Ludios, and I don't think it existed in this game. I
didn't need the money though, as at the end i had a naked AC of
-4. Ludios would have made the game even more "Monty Haul".

Gehennom was simple, apart from a scary encounter with Demogorgon. I
liked the relative lack of maze levels, and found the water and lava mazes
an interesting addition. I marked the  vibrating square on either
side with scrolls. Apart from Demo, none of the Demon Lords (Princes?)
gave any real trouble. Neither Vlad nor Frankenstein gave any
difficulty. Although there was a nasty moment in Vlad's tower when a
Vampire mage made a pool of water below me. (An example of slashem's
gratuitous nastiness).

I went up and down the dungeon a bit, consolidating my stash and
equipment and digging passages through Gehennom. After waking Rodney,
I killed him only 5 times, and the walk up the dungeon with the Amulet
was uneventful. The "mysterious force" with the amulet does not appear
in slashem, and I am not sorry to miss it. I used the Orb of Weight to
find the portals on the planes.  On astral I went to the left, where
famine died quickly. This was the neutral alter, so I offered the
amulet and breathed a sigh of relief.

Sacrificing gave me a lot of junk artifacts, but I settled on
two-weaponing Mjollnir and Vorpal Blade. I was without a BoH for a
long time, until I found one in the Black Market at about 6500
Zorkmids. Most of my wishes were on magic markers, and rounding out my
ascension kit (also replacing speed-boots lost to lava). I found a
second wand of wishing after the castle in Frankenstein's lab. I
experiment with a "blessed figurine of an Archon" in the Black Market,
hoping that I could make the Archon kill Sam with conflict. Sam killed
the Archon, so I gave up trying to rob the black market.

A red dragon gave me RDSM. I got GDSM from the nightmare level, after
source-diving informed me that there was a GDSM there. I forgot that
it was -9. The worry about magic resistance was ill-founded as every
vampire seemed to drop a cloak of magic resistance.

One thing about slashem is the "monty-haul" nature of the dungeon. All
those special branches gave up an enormous amount of loot. In addition
some items seem rather over-powered and guaranteed. e.g. Hungerless
regeneration from the almost-guaranteed Hand of Vecna.

I have been burned too many times in slashem by YASDs from Gugs, ghoul
queens, Vampire Mages etc. so this time I was not bothered about 
genociding many nasty monsters. Giant fleas seemed to multiply 
infinitely to fill the level (is this a bug?), so I genocided "a". 
L,h,;,Z,V went, also asphynxes and basilisks.

The two scariest moments in the game were nearly YASDs. Firstly I was
in the castle, when a Deva summoned some snakes. An ashynx was among
them and I started slowing down. I had just put all comestibles
(including lizard corpses) into my BoH, and had just prayed. ARg!
Fortunately I was able to retrieve a lizard corpse and eat it before
all was lost. Shortly after this I genocided asphynxes. Secondly was
Demogorgon. I had unwisely descended burdened into Gehennom, and then
Demogorgon appeared before me and starting whacking and stinging
me. Constantly applying my +6 unicorn horn, I eventually got a turn
in. I used it to invoke the Orb of Weight, to take me to level 2 (in
case I needed to pray). I applied the unicorn horn until I had a free
turn. Then I wished for a cockatrice corpse and Demogorgon was a
statue.

I was lucky to find an early alter, and some early good armor. After
reaching dungeon level 20 or so, having RDSM, and Mjollnir, I felt
that nothing could really kill me, barring YASD, and so it proved. In
this game I ensured I had all the equipment I wanted, quaffed a load
of !oFH and nearly maxed-out armour. After genociding so many things
this was probably overkill, but I was guarding against possible future
carelessness.


